    "engine": "jupyter",
    "markdown": "---\ngd-head-tags:\n  - >-\n    `<script type=\"application/ld+json\">[{\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"SoftwareSourceCode\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\", \"description\":\n    \"High-performance graph analysis library\", \"codeRepository\":\n    \"https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase\", \"license\":\n    \"https://opensource.org/licenses/MIT\", \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"documentation\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase\", \"programmingLanguage\": {\"@type\":\n    \"ComputerLanguage\", \"name\": \"Python\"}}, {\"@context\": \"https://schema.org\",\n    \"@type\": \"WebPage\", \"name\": \"Graph.add_turan_graph - EdgeCase\", \"isPartOf\":\n    {\"@type\": \"WebSite\", \"name\": \"EdgeCase\"}, \"url\":\n    \"https://rich-iannone.github.io/edgecase/reference/Graph.add_turan_graph.html\"}]</script>`{=html}\nopen-graph:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_turan_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add a Turán graph T(n, r) to the current graph.\ntwitter-card:\n  title: >-\n    [Graph.add_turan_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n    .doc-label-method} | EdgeCase\n  description: Add a Turán graph T(n, r) to the current graph.\ntitle: >-\n  [Graph.add_turan_graph()]{.doc-object-name .doc-function .doc-label\n  .doc-label-method}\nbody-classes: doc-api-page doc-py-api-page\nshift-heading-level-by: 0\nbread-crumbs: false\ntoc-depth: 3\ndescription-meta: Add a Turán graph T(n, r) to the current graph.\npage-navigation: false\nhtml-table-processing: none\n---\n\n::: {.doc-subject}\n\nAdd a Turán graph T(n, r) to the current graph.\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-usage-source}\nUsage\n\n[Source](https://github.com/rich-iannone/edgecase/blob/main/python/edgecase/graph.py#L8927-L9058){target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\"}\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-signature .doc-function}\n```pythonsignature\nGraph.add_turan_graph(\n    n,\n    r,\n    type=None,\n    label=True,\n    rel=None,\n    part_attr=\"part\",\n)\n```\n:::\n\n::: {.doc-text}\n\n![Turán graph](../assets/graphs/add-turan-graph.light.svg){.lightbox fig-alt=\"Three Turán graphs on a ring of seven nodes for r=2, 3, and 4 parts, each part in its own color. The seven nodes are split into parts as equal as possible (4 and 3; 3, 2, and 2; 2, 2, 2, and 1) and every pair of nodes in different parts is joined, so the graph gains edges as r grows (12, 16, and 18).\" width=\"100%\"}\n\nThe Turán graph splits `n` nodes into `r` groups whose sizes differ by at most one and\njoins every pair of nodes in different groups. It is the complete multipartite graph with\nthe most edges among all graphs on `n` nodes that contain no clique of `r + 1` nodes;\nTurán's theorem says no `K(r+1)`-free graph on `n` nodes has more edges.\n\nThe smaller groups (`n // r` nodes) come first and the larger ones (`n // r + 1` nodes)\nlast, each as a consecutive run of node IDs, and each node's group index is stored in\nthe `part_attr=` node attribute. In a directed graph every edge points from the\nearlier-created node to the later one. The graph is appended without touching or\nconnecting to existing nodes, and the whole construction is recorded as a single step.\n\nTurán graphs are useful for:\n\n- extremal graph theory: they are the densest graphs without a `K(r+1)` clique\n- test cases for clique, coloring, and independent-set algorithms (the clique number and\n  chromatic number are both `r` when `n >= r`)\n- balanced \"everyone except your own group\" relations, such as matches between equal\n  teams\n:::\n\n## Parameters {.doc-parameters}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code>[n]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Total number of nodes. Must be at least `1`.\n\n<code>[r]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [int]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Number of groups. Must satisfy `1 <= r <= n`. `r=1` gives `n` isolated nodes and\n    `r=n` gives the complete graph.\n\n<code>[type]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `type` attribute of every new node. If `None` (default),\n    no `type` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[label]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [bool]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[True]{.va}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   If `True` (default), each new node is labelled with its node ID as a string; a label\n    that is already used raises `ValueError` before anything is added. If `False`, the\n    nodes are left unlabelled.\n\n<code>[rel]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [None]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Optional value stored in the `rel` attribute of every new edge. If `None` (default),\n    no `rel` attribute is set.\n\n<code>[part_attr]{.doc-parameter-name}[:]{.doc-parameter-annotation-sep} [Optional[str]]{.doc-parameter-annotation} [=]{.doc-parameter-default-sep .op} [[&quot;part&quot;]{.st}]{.doc-parameter-default}</code>\n\n:   Name of the node attribute that records each node's group index. Default is\n    `\"part\"`. Pass `None` to skip storing it.\n:::\n\n## Returns {.doc-returns}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [Graph]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   Self for method chaining. The graph is modified in place.\n:::\n\n## Raises {.doc-raises}\n\n::: {.doc-definition-items}\n<code> [ValueError]{.doc-parameter-annotation}</code>\n\n:   If `n=` is less than `1`, or `r=` is not between `1` and `n=`.\n:::\n\n## See Also {.doc-see-also}\n\n[](`~add_complete_multipartite_graph`) \n\n:   Add a complete multipartite graph.\n\n[](`~add_full_graph`) \n\n:   Add a complete graph.\n\n[](`~clique_number`) \n\n:   Compute the size of a largest clique.\n\n## Examples {.doc-examples}\n\nThe Turán graph `T(n, r)` splits `n` nodes into `r` groups as equal in size as possible and\njoins every two nodes in different groups. `T(7, 3)` has groups of `2`, `2` and `3`:\n\n::: {#fb527cfd .cell execution_count=1}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\nimport edgecase as ec\n\ngraph = ec.Graph().add_turan_graph(n=7, r=3)\n\ngraph.get_node_df()[\"part\"].value_counts().sort(\"part\")\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=1}\n```{=html}\n<div><style>\n.dataframe > thead > tr,\n.dataframe > tbody > tr {\n  text-align: right;\n  white-space: pre-wrap;\n}\n</style>\n<small>shape: (3, 2)</small><table border=\"1\" class=\"dataframe\"><thead><tr><th>part</th><th>count</th></tr><tr><td>i64</td><td>u32</td></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>0</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>1</td><td>2</td></tr><tr><td>2</td><td>3</td></tr></tbody></table></div>\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\nOf all graphs on `n` nodes with no clique of `r + 1` nodes, the Turán graph has the most\nedges. For 7 nodes and no four nodes all joined to each other, that's 16:\n\n::: {#4e57e2e0 .cell execution_count=2}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ngraph.count_edges(), graph.clique_number()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=2}\n```\n(16, 3)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n### Two groups and four\n\n`T(8, 2)` on the left is `K(4, 4)`, with 16 edges and no triangle. `T(8, 4)` on the right\nhas four groups of two and 24 edges, and its largest cliques have four nodes:\n\n::: {#9e8fdee5 .cell execution_count=3}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntwo = ec.Graph().add_turan_graph(n=8, r=2)\nfour = ec.Graph().add_turan_graph(n=8, r=4)\n\ntwo.count_edges(), four.count_edges(), four.clique_number()\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=3}\n```\n(16, 24, 4)\n```\n:::\n:::\n\n\n::: {layout-ncol=\"2\"}\n\n::: {#46922acf .cell execution_count=4}\n``` {.python .cell-code}\ntwo.layout_circular().plot(\n    layout=\"pos\", color_by=\"part\", label_by=\"label\",\n    width=320, height=320, legend=False,\n)\n```\n\n::: {.cell-output .cell-output-display execution_count=4}\n```{=html}\n<div class=\"ec-theme\" style=\"display:contents\"><style class=\"ec-theme-vars\">:where(.ec-theme){--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}@media (prefers-color-scheme: dark){.ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}}:is(html.quarto-light, body.quarto-light, html[data-bs-theme=\"light\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"true\"], body.vscode-light, body.vscode-high-contrast-light, html[theme=\"light\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#fafafa;--ect-e5dfd507:#94a3b8;--ect-8a2de1d4:#374151;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(15,23,42,0.88);--ect-21ade003:#f1f5f9;--ect-61169ea5:#c2410c;--ect-f59ba8df:#a1a1aa}:is(html.quarto-dark, body.quarto-dark, html[data-bs-theme=\"dark\"], [data-jp-theme-light=\"false\"], body.vscode-dark, body.vscode-high-contrast:not(.vscode-high-contrast-light), html[theme=\"dark\"]) .ec-theme{--ect-3239c383:#0d1117;--ect-e5dfd507:#4b5563;--ect-8a2de1d4:#d1d5db;--ect-57425a7e:rgba(241,245,249,0.92);--ect-21ade003:#0f172a;--ect-61169ea5:#f97316;--ect-f59ba8df:#71717a}</style><div class=\"ec-plot\" style=\"position:relative;width:fit-content;max-width:100%;margin:1em auto\">\n<style>.ec-plot > svg { display:block; max-width:100%; height:auto; }</style>\n<svg xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/2000/svg\" width=\"320\" height=\"320\" viewBox=\"4.0 14.0 312.0 312.0\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', Arial, sans-serif;\">\n<rect x=\"4.0\" y=\"14.0\" width=\"312.0\" height=\"312.0\" fill=\"var(--ect-3239c383)\"/>\n<line x1=\"104.1\" y1=\"224.6\" x2=\"245.2\" y2=\"166.1\" stroke=\"var(--ect